From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:10:13 +0000
Subject: Add an AMOLED black theme

Settings > Theme gets a switch, "AMOLED black", off by default. While
the browser is dark (the Dark theme, or System default while the system
is dark), the browser's own screens use true black instead of dark gray:
toolbar, status and navigation bars, tab switcher, new tab page, menus,
dialogs, bottom sheets and settings.
The address field, cards and search boxes, including the settings
search field, keep a dark gray one step above black, so their edges stay
visible. Incognito screens and separate incognito windows are always
dark, so they turn black whenever the switch is on.

Under the switch, the checkbox "Material You colors" (Android 12 and
later, checked by default, usable only while the switch is on) chooses
the accent colors of the black theme. Checked uses the wallpaper colors.
Unchecked uses the browser's baseline palette. While the black theme is
active, a color picked in the new tab page customization is not used.
With the switch off, that color works as before.

Wallpaper colors already follow Android's color contrast setting on
Android 14 and later. With the baseline palette, medium and high
contrast use the Material 3 contrast color roles of that palette, and a
contrast listener recreates the affected screens when the setting
changes.

The theme is a set of theme overlays applied when an activity is
created, after the wallpaper colors. Views that are prepared ahead of
time for a custom tab record the AMOLED black state they were built
with: the switch, dark mode, the palette choice and the contrast level.
They are used only if the custom tab has the same state; otherwise the
custom tab builds its views as it does without prepared views. Changing
either setting recreates the open activities, as a theme change does.
Both values are stored in the browser's own preferences, and both rows
can be found in settings search. Web content is not affected: the color
scheme reported to sites still follows the Dark setting as before, and
no media feature or web API changes.

